sentences.text:
(i) The conviction under Section 7/16(1)(a)(i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act is maintained and sentence is modified to the extent that he shall undergo a simple imprisonment of six months;
(ii) The conviction under Section 7/16(1)(a)(ii) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act is maintained and the sentence is modified to the extent that he shall undergo imprisonment of three months only;
(iii) The sentence of fine shall remain as it is;
(iv) Both the sentence shall run concurrently;
(v) The period of imprisonment already undergone by the revisionist shall be set off in the substantive sentence of imprisonment imposed by this Court.
9.

opennyai_summary.decision:
8. In view of all the above reasons, in my opinion the imposing of one year of rigorous imprisonment is too harsh in the circumstances of this case, hence, while maintaining the conviction, sentence order is accordingly modified as below:-
(i) The conviction under Section 7/16(1)(a)(i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act is maintained and sentence is modified to the extent that he shall undergo a simple imprisonment of six months;
(ii) The conviction under Section 7/16(1)(a)(ii) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act is maintained and the sentence is modified to the extent that he shall undergo imprisonment of three months only;
(iii) The sentence of fine shall remain as it is;
(iv) Both the sentence shall run concurrently;
(v) The period of imprisonment already undergone by the revisionist shall be set off in the substantive sentence of imprisonment imposed by this Court.
9.
Accordingly, this criminal revision is disposed of.
10. Copy of this order be immediately transmitted to the court concerned for necessary action.

